      "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept. Production sprite animation expansion for original hand-drawn 2D dark fantasy insect game. Reference images are identity and style references only, NOT desired grid or background. Preserve exact character identity, proportions, costume, palette, clean ink and painterly material textures. Pure side view all living frames facing RIGHT. Transparent real alpha background, no backdrop, ground, shadows, labels, text, borders, particles, panels. Each equal cell contains exactly one COMPLETE character including every antenna, blade and robe, with ample transparent gutter. Fixed body scale and centered pelvis, grounded foot baseline at 90% cell height. Distinct redrawn poses with real limb and weapon articulation, never stamp, shift or rotate a whole copy. Character Moss Bell Matriarch exactly reference: ivory mantis mask, branching antennae with hanging tiny bronze bells, engraved bronze bell torso, flowering moss root cloak, paired ivory scythe forearms. SPARSE FOUR columns by FOUR rows =16 complete sprites, square canvas. Each full sprite maximum 55% cell width and height so great transparent gaps remain, no physical touch between cells. Same scale throughout. ROW1 four heavy attack key poses: twin scythes overhead, downward arc, low ground impact crouch, rising followthrough. ROW2 four cast key poses: fold arms toward bell chest, open first arm, open both scythes wide while bell torso leans, settle. ROW3 four phase attack key poses: low root cloak crouch, scythe forward lunge, wide paired slash fully extended, torso recoils. ROW4 four sequential death poses: standing stagger head droops, kneeling body compressed, falling onto right side, fully collapsed root robe with both scythes visible. All right facing complete side view hand drawn sprites on true alpha. No separate effects, background, shadows, text or floor.",
